is a really prominent bugaboo in Australian folklore, and might make
for an interesting bugaboo in Nethack.

"Descriptions of bunyips vary wildly. It is usually given as a sort of
lake monster. Common features in Aboriginal drawings include a horse-
like tail, flippers, and walrus-like tusks or horns. According to
legend they are said to lurk in swamps, billabongs, creeks, riverbeds
and waterholes. At night their blood-curdling cries can be heard as
they devour any animal that ventures near their abodes."

Something about the name sounds frightening and comical at the same
time to me. I know if I were hopping across Juiblex's swamp and
suddenly saw a green q surface from the water, I'd jump. =)

I'm not sure what exactly a Bunyip  "should" look like, or how a
Nethack bunyip "should" behave, so I'll leave both to your vivid
imaginations...


